poses of paying back the money and  for purposes of maintaining this and  kind of getting the money in the first  place right I mean you you can always  borrow but if there are firms that are  willing to build roads or expand Road  capacity or take over water treatment  they're putting in a lot of the money  right  well yeah further they are willing to  put money into equity they want to  partially own these assets those same  firms are saying look I'll maintain that  asset for 20 years you don't have to  worry about me building it in an  inferior way so that the cost of  maintenance is transferred to the public  sector and and also in terms of water  and wastewater Airport privatization  alike we see great new revenue sources  that can be produced to help pay back  those fines that one of the biggest  lifts though I mean it seems to me it's  kind of like the shift from free TV to  cable TV you know it's hard to do and  now nobody would ever go back to free TV  I mean but is that it I mean is there a  turn there that we have to make that's  going to be hard to do well it will be  hard to do because there's a lot of  support in to the status quo right if  anybody had any idea how inefficiently  the public sector does capital assets  and I don't mean corruptly I just mean  efficiently so you you have a long  procurement to hire somebody to design  it long procurement hire somebody to  build it then somebody has to maintain  it probably the government right there  handoffs to each of those areas and so  all of those handoffs all that  inefficiency can become more efficient a  public-private partnership says here's  the here's the scope of what we want  the mayor says you tell me how you're  going to build it how you can maintain  it how you're going to finance it I'll  decide whether the service levels are  right the fares are right the fees or  the tolls and the services right well  we'll leave it there thanks so much for  talking to us Mayor Stephen Goldsmith  the recipient of the 2017 Reason  Foundation Sophos award thank you very  much for reason I'm Nick Gillespie  [Music]

